---
import FeynmanStory from "./FeynmanStory.astro";
---

<details class="flower-disclosure" id="flower-story">
  <summary class="specimen" aria-label="Why a flower? Read the Feynman passage">
    <span class="specimen-top">
      <span class="eyebrow">A flower, and a closer look</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">Fig. 01</span>
    </span>
    <svg
      viewBox="0 0 460 400"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="flower-title"
      class="flower-art"
    >
      <title id="flower-title">A botanical flower illustration with an optional view of its underlying geometry</title>
      <defs>
        <pattern id="dots" width="20" height="20" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <circle cx="1" cy="1" r=".7" fill="#7e8c76" opacity=".23" />
        </pattern>
      </defs>
      <rect width="460" height="400" fill="url(#dots)" />
      <g class="flower-stem" fill="none" stroke="#536650" stroke-width="2">
        <path d="M228 189 C214 247 251 296 225 374" />
        <path
          d="M233 296 C201 294 170 265 162 240 C204 243 228 263 233 296Z"
          fill="#bac4a9"
        />
        <path
          d="M233 320 C266 309 285 276 287 258 C254 263 237 284 233 320Z"
          fill="#a9b798"
        />
        <path d="M163 241L232 295 M286 259L235 318" stroke-width="1" />
      </g>
      <g transform="translate(227 165)" stroke="#65775e" stroke-width="1.2">
        {Array.from({ length: 13 }, (_, i) => (
          <ellipse
            cx="0"
            cy="-54"
            rx="22"
            ry="59"
            transform={`rotate(${(i * 360) / 13})`}
            fill={i % 2 ? "#d9dfc7" : "#e6e7d4"}
            fill-opacity=".88"
          />
        ))}
        <circle r="33" fill="#9aa682" />
        {Array.from({ length: 100 }, (_, i) => {
          const a = i * 2.39996;
          const r = 2.8 * Math.sqrt(i);
          return (
            <circle
              cx={Math.cos(a) * r}
              cy={Math.sin(a) * r}
              r="1.65"
              fill="#4d604a"
              stroke="none"
            />
          );
        })}
      </g>
      <g class="structure" fill="none" stroke="#8b634d" stroke-width="1">
        <circle cx="227" cy="165" r="115" stroke-dasharray="3 5" />
        <circle cx="227" cy="165" r="65" />
        <path d="M90 165H365 M227 28V301" stroke-dasharray="3 5" />
        <path d="M264 120L325 67H402 M258 188L337 220H410" />
        <text
          x="323"
          y="58"
          fill="#715340"
          stroke="none"
          font-size="11"
          font-family="monospace"
        >
          form & pattern
        </text>
        <text
          x="336"
          y="238"
          fill="#715340"
          stroke="none"
          font-size="11"
          font-family="monospace"
        >
          a closer look
        </text>
      </g>
      <text
        x="26"
        y="367"
        font-family="Georgia,serif"
        font-style="italic"
        font-size="16"
        fill="#62715b"
      >
        Inspired by Feynman’s flower.
      </text>
    </svg>
    <span class="specimen-bottom">
      <span class="flower-caption">There’s a story behind this.</span>
      <span class="flower-invitation">
        Why a flower? <span class="disclosure-sign" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </span>
    </span>
  </summary>
  <div class="flower-story prose">
    <h2>About that flower.</h2>
    <p>
      This is probably the closest someone else has come to explaining how I
      feel about things.
    </p>
    <FeynmanStory />
    <p>
      I like that understanding something doesn’t have to take away the feeling.
      You can enjoy a song and wonder how it was made. You can look at the sky
      and want to understand what’s out there. For me, the questions are part of
      the enjoyment.
    </p>
    <button type="button" class="text-link flower-close">
      ↑ Back to the flower
    </button>
  </div>
</details>
<script>
  const story = document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>("#flower-story");
  story?.classList.add("is-enhanced");
  const close = story?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(".flower-close");
  close?.addEventListener("click", () => {
    if (!story) return;
    story.open = false;
    story.querySelector("summary")?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
    story.scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest", behavior: "instant" });
  });
</script>
